01:07:19.770 --> 01:07:23.391
[SPEAKER_01]: How long has the alcohol been depleted?

01:07:24.432 --> 01:07:25.412
[SPEAKER_00]: It's been about a week.

01:07:26.432 --> 01:07:27.153
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, damn.

01:07:28.153 --> 01:07:28.473
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

01:07:29.622 --> 01:07:33.265
[SPEAKER_01]: No sources that you've been able to secure?

01:07:34.986 --> 01:07:43.652
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, actually, that's kind of where Karmirg and Gouge are now.

01:07:44.593 --> 01:07:51.057
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't say anything about it, but they're looking at trying to get more supplies from Westkeep.

01:07:55.320 --> 01:07:56.521
[SPEAKER_01]: That's a little bit farther out.

01:07:57.554 --> 01:08:02.477
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you think if I send my man out to Ansar that he might be able to secure some food for gold?

01:08:03.718 --> 01:08:05.239
[SPEAKER_00]: Possibly at the Fisher Village.

01:08:05.999 --> 01:08:06.299
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

01:08:06.499 --> 01:08:07.380
[SPEAKER_00]: I've done that too.

01:08:07.500 --> 01:08:08.621
[SPEAKER_00]: Port Colm as well.

01:08:11.422 --> 01:08:12.863
[SPEAKER_00]: They're not as effective as we are.

01:08:13.844 --> 01:08:14.264
[SPEAKER_00]: Of course.

01:08:14.424 --> 01:08:16.065
[SPEAKER_00]: Not everybody can do that though.

01:08:19.387 --> 01:08:23.510
[SPEAKER_01]: So you had referred to others besides just the Toli rats.

01:08:26.667 --> 01:08:27.707
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you want to go to your back room?

01:08:31.528 --> 01:08:31.908
[SPEAKER_00]: All right.

01:08:33.228 --> 01:08:34.768
[SPEAKER_00]: There's nothing really here to steal.

01:08:35.969 --> 01:08:36.209
What the?

01:08:36.989 --> 01:08:38.549
[SPEAKER_01]: I wouldn't say that.

01:08:38.609 --> 01:08:41.129
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a decent place.

01:08:41.429 --> 01:08:48.711
[SPEAKER_00]: No, the only thing these rabble would try to steal is my alcohol, but unfortunately I have none.

01:08:48.851 --> 01:08:50.551
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yes, let's go in the back room.

01:08:51.111 --> 01:08:54.272
[SPEAKER_00]: Have a little chat.

01:08:54.412 --> 01:08:56.012
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, he looks across and goes,

01:08:56.967 --> 01:09:08.772
[SPEAKER_00]: Not if you take anything and the two of you walk back into the kitchen, which basically is pretty bare, right?

01:09:10.093 --> 01:09:10.453
[SPEAKER_01]: Damn.

01:09:10.913 --> 01:09:11.293
[SPEAKER_01]: All right.

01:09:13.094 --> 01:09:13.454
[SPEAKER_01]: All right.

01:09:14.935 --> 01:09:17.816
[SPEAKER_01]: So, this seems pretty dire here.

01:09:17.836 --> 01:09:21.738
[SPEAKER_01]: Are you even able to put much on the table for these fellas out there?

01:09:22.343 --> 01:09:28.444
[SPEAKER_00]: They don't come here for the food, they come here for the patrons looking for, you know, them.

01:09:29.205 --> 01:09:31.005
[SPEAKER_00]: They're what's for sale, more than anything.

01:09:32.265 --> 01:09:36.146
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I'm surprised every mercenary hasn't been snatched up already by the princes.

01:09:36.726 --> 01:09:42.208
[SPEAKER_00]: But I guess if they can't sally for... Oh, you'd be surprised, actually.

01:09:43.588 --> 01:09:48.749
[SPEAKER_00]: Princes, nobles, merchants, those are usually the people that hire these men.

01:09:49.230 --> 01:09:50.870
[SPEAKER_00]: But without the great market working,

01:09:52.027 --> 01:09:57.971
[SPEAKER_00]: It's hard for these sellswords to find a decent day of pay.

01:10:02.874 --> 01:10:04.615
[SPEAKER_01]: Is it the same all over the city?

01:10:06.516 --> 01:10:12.460
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, I would say the Noble District has more than its fair share, of course.

01:10:13.621 --> 01:10:15.342
[SPEAKER_00]: Military doesn't look too bad off.

01:10:16.223 --> 01:10:17.664
[SPEAKER_00]: Merchants, of course, are fat.

01:10:17.764 --> 01:10:19.385
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm sure that their larders are all

01:10:20.340 --> 01:10:22.120
[SPEAKER_00]: Decently filled, actually.

01:10:25.941 --> 01:10:29.382
[SPEAKER_00]: No one knows how long this is gonna last, though, so no one's really selling.

01:10:30.402 --> 01:10:43.184
[SPEAKER_01]: What is the word on the street as to why the Sea Princes haven't sallied for us and kicked the crap out of Gradsfield?

01:10:43.484 --> 01:10:48.485
[SPEAKER_00]: The word on the street is that Lord Jamis is a coward, but you and I know that's not true.

01:10:49.759 --> 01:11:01.641
[SPEAKER_00]: I've heard the rumors, and by the way, Gouge and Karmirg have talked in my presence a few times.

01:11:01.741 --> 01:11:04.261
[SPEAKER_00]: There's totally spies around, believe you me.

01:11:07.502 --> 01:11:13.023
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, you said there's been an increase in others.

01:11:14.143 --> 01:11:15.723
[SPEAKER_01]: Have you seen an increase in Suu?

01:11:17.664 --> 01:11:18.984
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, definitely.

01:11:20.344 --> 01:11:20.965
[SPEAKER_00]: Definitely.

01:11:21.245 --> 01:11:23.569
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the Toli are crawling through the city.

01:11:24.169 --> 01:11:32.301
[SPEAKER_00]: And in fact, I don't know if you've known this, the Gouge and Kalmar ran into six of them at one point, killed many of them.

01:11:33.303 --> 01:11:34.644
[SPEAKER_00]: Out on the docks, no less.

01:11:38.042 --> 01:11:39.443
[SPEAKER_01]: At broad daylight or at nighttime?

01:11:39.463 --> 01:11:40.504
[SPEAKER_00]: No, it was at nighttime.

01:11:40.544 --> 01:11:48.669
[SPEAKER_00]: They were protecting some fool who had sailed into town, was flashing his money all over the place.

01:11:49.189 --> 01:11:58.715
[SPEAKER_00]: Some crazy Keog Suel, supposedly from Gradsul.

01:11:59.255 --> 01:12:03.318
[SPEAKER_00]: Anyway, asking a lot of questions, making himself very well known.

01:12:04.258 --> 01:12:04.979
[SPEAKER_00]: Kind of a fool.

01:12:06.179 --> 01:12:06.860
[SPEAKER_00]: But apparently,

01:12:08.458 --> 01:12:10.021
[SPEAKER_00]: He got the attention of the Toli.

01:12:10.041 --> 01:12:15.753
[SPEAKER_00]: Steve?

01:14:07.876 --> 01:14:08.376
[SPEAKER_00]: Hey, I'm here.

01:14:09.157 --> 01:14:09.857
[SPEAKER_01]: All right, cool.

01:14:09.877 --> 01:14:11.218
[SPEAKER_01]: Sorry, I had to run to the bathroom real quick.

01:14:11.238 --> 01:14:11.979
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

01:14:13.600 --> 01:14:14.140
[SPEAKER_01]: All right.

01:14:16.101 --> 01:14:20.704
[SPEAKER_01]: So we have Suel and Toli here, crawling all over the city.

01:14:22.846 --> 01:14:28.329
[SPEAKER_01]: You've been privy to some of Gouge and Karmirg's conversations.

01:14:30.511 --> 01:14:31.811
[SPEAKER_01]: Where do you think I can help best?

01:14:33.593 --> 01:14:34.133
[SPEAKER_01]: Help what?

01:14:35.720 --> 01:14:41.242
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't know, gouging Karnberg, isn't that what I always end up doing, is bailing their ass out of some sort of bullshit or the other?

01:14:42.162 --> 01:14:43.863
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, well, that's for sure.

01:14:43.883 --> 01:14:51.405
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't know, some young lass has been coming in and talking to them, hiring them for jobs every now and then.

01:14:51.425 --> 01:14:52.745
[SPEAKER_00]: Hmm.

01:14:54.166 --> 01:14:58.967
[SPEAKER_01]: Maybe point her out if she comes in, that I happen to be down in the common room or something.

01:14:59.187 --> 01:15:01.808
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, you can't miss her, she's one of your kind.

01:15:02.848 --> 01:15:02.928
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh.

01:15:02.948 --> 01:15:03.909
[SPEAKER_01]: What else?

01:15:04.609 --> 01:15:04.789
[SPEAKER_01]: Huh.

01:15:05.774 --> 01:15:06.054
[SPEAKER_01]: Pretty?

01:15:07.275 --> 01:15:07.395
[SPEAKER_00]: Eh.

01:15:08.875 --> 01:15:12.257
[SPEAKER_00]: I've seen prettier, but, yeah, she's not bad to look at.

01:15:13.497 --> 01:15:16.239
[SPEAKER_01]: She's not plump like you like?

01:15:17.459 --> 01:15:18.700
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, not even close.

01:15:18.760 --> 01:15:19.560
[SPEAKER_00]: She's a wood elf.

01:15:23.262 --> 01:15:24.842
[SPEAKER_00]: Very skinny, like yourself.

01:15:27.283 --> 01:15:30.185
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, we both know you don't fight.

01:15:36.993 --> 01:15:38.593
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I can blow things up really well.

01:15:38.873 --> 01:15:42.814
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, that has more utility in most cases.

01:15:42.834 --> 01:15:46.015
[SPEAKER_00]: You could probably get yourself a job with the Navy if you wanted to.

01:15:46.035 --> 01:15:49.516
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm sure they are looking for someone with your skills.

01:15:50.056 --> 01:15:50.576
[SPEAKER_00]: You need it.

01:15:51.716 --> 01:15:53.817
[SPEAKER_01]: If I need it, I may.

01:15:54.057 --> 01:15:55.557
[SPEAKER_01]: We can't get booze in this place.

01:15:56.637 --> 01:16:01.378
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, like I said, there's no work escorting nobles or merchants anymore.

01:16:02.238 --> 01:16:03.159
[SPEAKER_00]: It's hard times.

01:16:04.399 --> 01:16:04.599
[SPEAKER_00]: So,

01:16:05.692 --> 01:16:11.134
[SPEAKER_01]: Have you, uh, any strong arms on your pay roster?

01:16:12.474 --> 01:16:13.895
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't pay those fools.

01:16:14.195 --> 01:16:14.955
[SPEAKER_00]: They pay me.

01:16:16.776 --> 01:16:21.237
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I'm just thinking in case some Lord look totally rats come back.

01:16:21.497 --> 01:16:22.778
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, don't worry about those.

01:16:23.398 --> 01:16:25.859
[SPEAKER_00]: Galgen Carmich will have their heads if they see them.

01:16:27.319 --> 01:16:29.400
[SPEAKER_00]: Apparently somebody's put a bounty on them.

01:16:31.329 --> 01:16:31.869
[SPEAKER_01]: On Toli?

01:16:32.370 --> 01:16:32.670
[SPEAKER_01]: Rats?

01:16:32.910 --> 01:16:35.131
[SPEAKER_01]: Or on foul gauchin karma?

01:16:35.151 --> 01:16:36.152
[SPEAKER_00]: No, the assassins.

01:16:36.312 --> 01:16:37.152
[SPEAKER_00]: The assassins.

01:16:38.173 --> 01:16:38.993
[SPEAKER_00]: They stand out.

01:16:39.033 --> 01:16:41.334
[SPEAKER_00]: You can tell them from a mile away.

01:16:43.015 --> 01:16:43.656
[SPEAKER_01]: Seriously?

01:16:44.016 --> 01:16:45.217
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh yes, absolutely.

01:16:46.057 --> 01:16:50.519
[SPEAKER_00]: Sewal, silk shirts, delicate swords and daggers.

01:16:51.360 --> 01:16:53.081
[SPEAKER_01]: They haven't even tried to disguise themselves.

01:16:53.981 --> 01:16:55.202
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, they didn't that night.

01:16:56.932 --> 01:17:00.376
[SPEAKER_00]: After that, though, what Gouge told me is somebody to put a prize on their heads.

01:17:01.317 --> 01:17:06.844
[SPEAKER_00]: And basically, he was told to kill them if he saw any of them in the city.

01:17:07.465 --> 01:17:09.487
[SPEAKER_00]: Since then, they've been nowhere.

01:17:10.749 --> 01:17:12.671
[SPEAKER_00]: Their spies are still around, however.

01:17:13.993 --> 01:17:16.776
[SPEAKER_01]: Their spies is obviously observable.

01:17:19.946 --> 01:17:21.887
[SPEAKER_00]: Not as obvious as you might think.

01:17:22.727 --> 01:17:31.330
[SPEAKER_00]: I heard tell that Lord Jamis actually had a spy in his own council.

01:17:32.231 --> 01:17:42.415
[SPEAKER_00]: In fact, from what Gouge told me, this man had been spying on Lord Jamis right under his nose for months.

01:17:44.636 --> 01:17:47.697
[SPEAKER_00]: Gouge took the man out at Lord Jamis' bequest.

01:17:56.491 --> 01:18:08.441
[SPEAKER_01]: If I need some eyes and ears on the streets to look for some of these spies, do you have any resources that you trust?

01:18:10.923 --> 01:18:11.884
[SPEAKER_00]: What are you looking for?

01:18:13.745 --> 01:18:14.286
[SPEAKER_01]: Spies.

01:18:16.988 --> 01:18:18.429
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, those are hard to come by.

01:18:18.449 --> 01:18:18.850
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean...

01:18:23.077 --> 01:18:27.198
[SPEAKER_00]: We could have the lads keep an eye out, if that's what you'd like.

01:18:28.258 --> 01:18:29.518
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, what do they need?

01:18:29.538 --> 01:18:31.199
[SPEAKER_01]: Do they need food or pay?

01:18:31.999 --> 01:18:33.459
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm sure food would go better.

01:18:33.479 --> 01:18:36.400
[SPEAKER_01]: Food would go better, of course.

01:18:36.700 --> 01:18:37.360
[SPEAKER_00]: At this point.

01:18:38.200 --> 01:18:39.921
[SPEAKER_00]: But exactly what are you looking for?

01:18:41.901 --> 01:18:46.082
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, more... more Suel assassins.

01:18:46.722 --> 01:18:50.423
[SPEAKER_01]: Of course, maybe more discreetly hid now.

01:18:51.709 --> 01:18:52.950
[SPEAKER_01]: Certainly anybody...

01:18:55.472 --> 01:19:08.183
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm looking to see... if they penetrated Lord, if some force, some spy, some Seul spy penetrated Lord Jamis' counsel.

01:19:09.884 --> 01:19:10.885
[SPEAKER_00]: He wasn't a Seul.

01:19:12.046 --> 01:19:12.466
[SPEAKER_01]: He wasn't?

01:19:12.666 --> 01:19:14.288
[SPEAKER_00]: He was an Oeridian, yes.

01:19:16.910 --> 01:19:19.092
[SPEAKER_00]: He's being paid off by a Seul, though.

01:19:20.148 --> 01:19:21.228
[SPEAKER_00]: Of course it wouldn't be that easy.

01:19:21.508 --> 01:19:22.908
[SPEAKER_00]: A Toli, no less.

01:19:24.909 --> 01:19:25.249
[SPEAKER_01]: Hmm.

01:19:27.069 --> 01:19:29.590
[SPEAKER_00]: But no, there are spies all over the place, from what I've heard.

01:19:29.610 --> 01:19:31.150
[SPEAKER_00]: From what Gow just told me.

01:19:31.890 --> 01:19:32.950
[SPEAKER_01]: You mean, uh, Toli?

01:19:33.270 --> 01:19:35.031
[SPEAKER_01]: Toli spies, or just spies?

01:19:35.991 --> 01:19:37.971
[SPEAKER_00]: They're not Toli, of course, Jude.

01:19:39.051 --> 01:19:40.432
[SPEAKER_00]: They're Oeridians, just like.

01:19:40.452 --> 01:19:43.132
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, it paid off by the Toli.

01:19:43.432 --> 01:19:44.072
[SPEAKER_00]: Absolutely.

01:19:44.092 --> 01:19:48.733
[SPEAKER_01]: Of course it wouldn't have been that easy, too.

01:19:50.414 --> 01:19:53.876
[SPEAKER_00]: In fact, I wouldn't be surprised if some of the men out there weren't on their payroll.

01:19:54.477 --> 01:19:55.557
[SPEAKER_00]: After what Gouge did.

01:19:55.577 --> 01:19:57.879
[SPEAKER_01]: Wait, what did Gouge do?

01:19:58.919 --> 01:20:00.100
[SPEAKER_00]: He killed their assassins.

01:20:00.460 --> 01:20:01.181
[SPEAKER_00]: I just told ya.

01:20:02.141 --> 01:20:03.582
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, I see what you mean.

01:20:03.622 --> 01:20:04.343
[SPEAKER_01]: Sorry, sorry.

01:20:06.584 --> 01:20:08.705
[SPEAKER_00]: No, it's a strange time.

01:20:08.765 --> 01:20:10.166
[SPEAKER_00]: People talking and so on.

01:20:14.569 --> 01:20:17.231
[SPEAKER_01]: So I'm surprised you don't have a still being operated.

01:20:17.831 --> 01:20:18.992
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, grain?

01:20:20.603 --> 01:20:20.923
[SPEAKER_01]: Rule?

01:20:21.404 --> 01:20:22.585
[SPEAKER_01]: Turning that into alcohol?

01:20:22.625 --> 01:20:23.946
[SPEAKER_01]: There's a mint to be made here.

01:20:24.906 --> 01:20:25.847
[SPEAKER_01]: A city under siege?

01:20:28.109 --> 01:20:28.409
[SPEAKER_00]: Well.

01:20:29.971 --> 01:20:35.255
[SPEAKER_00]: If I had the knowledge to do that, I'd do it, but unfortunately I'm not a man of those means.

01:20:36.175 --> 01:20:36.356
[SPEAKER_01]: Hmm.

01:20:37.817 --> 01:20:39.398
[SPEAKER_01]: What do you know of a mad alchemist?

01:20:41.820 --> 01:20:42.000
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh.

01:20:42.020 --> 01:20:44.042
[SPEAKER_01]: The one that's out in the square.

01:20:44.082 --> 01:20:45.943
[SPEAKER_01]: The merchant in the square.

01:20:45.963 --> 01:20:46.784
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, I know him.

01:20:48.025 --> 01:20:48.986
[SPEAKER_01]: You might be able to, like,

01:20:49.978 --> 01:20:50.518
[SPEAKER_01]: Copped us.

01:20:51.899 --> 01:20:56.800
[SPEAKER_01]: If food's on such short supply, perhaps we could invite him here, if I can secure some food.

01:20:57.620 --> 01:21:00.621
[SPEAKER_00]: That man never leaves his building.

01:21:01.701 --> 01:21:04.041
[SPEAKER_01]: No, he has a building on the square.

01:21:04.502 --> 01:21:05.782
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh yes, you know this.

01:21:06.722 --> 01:21:07.242
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't do it.

01:21:07.722 --> 01:21:08.443
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh yeah, you do.

01:21:08.583 --> 01:21:12.724
[SPEAKER_00]: This guy is like a... he's got a curio shop.

01:21:12.824 --> 01:21:13.784
[SPEAKER_01]: Very well known.

01:21:14.064 --> 01:21:16.124
[SPEAKER_01]: So he's mad crazy, but he's got his own place.

01:21:16.324 --> 01:21:17.585
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, so he's not like a...

01:21:19.408 --> 01:21:21.248
[SPEAKER_00]: He is not indigent at all.

01:21:21.428 --> 01:21:23.229
[SPEAKER_00]: He's actually very wealthy.

01:21:23.969 --> 01:21:28.470
[SPEAKER_00]: And he basically makes money selling healing potions and shit like that to people.

01:21:29.750 --> 01:21:30.070
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

01:21:33.891 --> 01:21:34.931
[SPEAKER_00]: But no, I think you're right.

01:21:34.971 --> 01:21:37.212
[SPEAKER_00]: I think getting him to make a still would be a good idea.

01:21:37.232 --> 01:21:39.732
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, I think so.

01:21:40.232 --> 01:21:44.153
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, it's gonna be gruel for days, weeks.

01:21:46.372 --> 01:21:50.173
[SPEAKER_01]: We could make more money if we were able to turn some of that into alcohol.

01:21:50.753 --> 01:21:53.114
[SPEAKER_01]: And, you know, people are never very hungry when they're drunk.

01:21:55.914 --> 01:21:56.435
[SPEAKER_00]: I agree.

01:21:58.715 --> 01:21:59.015
[SPEAKER_01]: All right.

01:21:59.895 --> 01:22:01.036
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll see what I can do tomorrow.

01:22:01.456 --> 01:22:02.176
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll move down there.

01:22:02.196 --> 01:22:03.056
[SPEAKER_01]: I need to talk to him.

01:22:03.836 --> 01:22:06.437
[SPEAKER_01]: So perhaps that will be a good beginning.

01:22:07.250 --> 01:22:10.291
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll keep my eye out for the last.

01:22:10.671 --> 01:22:11.971
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll tell you when she comes in.

01:22:12.471 --> 01:22:18.793
[SPEAKER_00]: She usually comes in and talks to Gouging Coburg, but she hasn't been around for the last few days, seeing they're out of town.

01:22:20.213 --> 01:22:30.876
[SPEAKER_01]: Perhaps you could employ a couple of the lads that you were talking about, and what I'd like to know is specifically some of the places and the haunts that people that come in and out of here go.

01:22:31.436 --> 01:22:35.657
[SPEAKER_01]: There's not a big number, so three or four of the lads, if we can provide them some food.

01:22:41.585 --> 01:22:42.346
[SPEAKER_01]: But I'd like to know.

01:22:42.606 --> 01:22:47.950
[SPEAKER_01]: If we have a spy in our midst out there, it's a given, as you said, probably.

01:22:48.150 --> 01:22:52.354
[SPEAKER_01]: But I'd like to know where they reside.

01:22:54.656 --> 01:22:54.776
[SPEAKER_00]: Ah.

01:22:55.356 --> 01:22:55.877
